Package: ems-appliance-manager
Version: 0.1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: EMS SolarFlow API Control <noreply@example.invalid>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), systemd, adduser, acl, iproute2, procps, util-linux,
 mount, ca-certificates, passwd, zstd, gpgv, openssh-client, cloud-guest-utils,
 e2fsprogs
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce, network-manager, openssh-server, openssh-sftp-server,
 avahi-daemon, avahi-utils, dosfstools
Homepage: https://github.com/basecubedev/ems-solarflow-api-control
Description: EMS SolarFlow Raspberry Pi Appliance Manager
 Host management and recovery for an EMS SolarFlow appliance. Runs as two
 systemd services outside Docker so it stays reachable when the EMS Admin
 container, the Docker daemon or EMS itself are unavailable.
 .
 An unprivileged web process serves the recovery UI; a privileged agent
 executes a fixed allowlist of typed host operations over a local Unix socket.
 It installs, verifies and rolls back the EMS Admin container, installs
 operating-system security updates, manages SSH public keys and the read-only
 backup account, and reports host status.
